<title>USA: HEI to buy back up to 250,000 shares.</title>
<headline>HEI to buy back up to 250,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>HEI Inc said Friday its board of directors authorized the repurchase of up to 250,000 of its common shares.</p>
<p>As of April 25, the company had 4,207,476 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The shares will be purchased from time to time, based upon market conditions and other business considerations at the discretion of management.</p>
<p>HEI designs and manufactures ultra-miniature microelectronic devices and high technology products incorporating those devices.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
